WEBVTT

00:07.549 --> 00:09.092
This is for the West Coast city

00:13.388 --> 00:14.264
Come on, Noah.

00:15.140 --> 00:18.059
Drive, drive, drive, drive! Hey, hey, hey!

00:18.143 --> 00:22.772
Let's go! That's my boy!
I taught him that.

00:24.065 --> 00:27.777
-Feels good to be present, doesn't it?
-When you right, you right.

00:31.740 --> 00:32.741
Come on, Noah.

00:38.955 --> 00:40.707
-Uh-uh.
-Defense!

00:40.790 --> 00:43.084
This nigga must be back
smoking sherm or something.

00:43.168 --> 00:46.337
-After the shit he pulled on Thanksgiving?
-I'm sure Noah invited him.

00:46.421 --> 00:48.715
He just wants
a relationship with his grandfather.

00:48.798 --> 00:51.843
Baby, you see these two men he brought in?
You know what they about?

00:51.926 --> 00:54.763
Okay, but can you focus
on our son Noah, please?

00:55.430 --> 00:58.516
Today's throwing up finger rolls.
Tomorrow, throwing up some gang's set.

00:58.600 --> 01:01.644
-Now Nightmare gotta get his ass up out.
-Hey, shush.

01:03.146 --> 01:05.523
It's all right, it's all right!
We'll get back in it.

01:05.607 --> 01:08.401
-Go, South Central. Y'all got it.
-Alright, buddy, come on.

01:08.485 --> 01:10.779
Go get 'em. All right.

01:20.580 --> 01:23.792
-What the fuck is he doing here?
-Coltrane Wilder?

01:23.875 --> 01:26.252
I don't know.
Passing out sneakers to kids?

01:26.336 --> 01:28.880
We'd like to take a moment
to thank Coltrane Wilder

01:28.963 --> 01:32.842
and Wilder Holdings
for their generous donation to both teams.

01:32.926 --> 01:35.386
Please don't tell me
you have a problem with him too.

01:35.470 --> 01:38.515
Nigga thinks he's
South Central Santa Claus and shit.

01:38.598 --> 01:41.601
Isaiah, please stop being so childish.

01:41.684 --> 01:43.186
His wife is my friend.

01:43.269 --> 01:45.522
And look at what he's doing.
Some of these kids need shoes.

01:45.605 --> 01:46.773
It's a sweet gesture.

01:46.856 --> 01:50.193
What could possibly be wrong with that?

01:50.276 --> 01:51.277
Hey.

01:53.321 --> 01:55.490
No, nothing? Just…

02:00.829 --> 02:02.789
-Hey.
-Mm-hmm.

02:08.294 --> 02:09.379
Come on, Noah!

02:09.462 --> 02:12.841
That's right, little man!
Put that punk on skates, boy!

02:13.842 --> 02:16.136
That's it, boy!
That's what I'm talking about.

02:16.219 --> 02:18.221
Future OG out there!

02:19.347 --> 02:21.224
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

02:23.977 --> 02:25.603
That's my baby!

02:38.741 --> 02:40.743
Hey, you peep OG in there?

02:40.827 --> 02:42.704
Wasn't that nigga
locked up with us in Lancaster?

02:42.787 --> 02:44.122
Mm-hmm. I remember him.

02:44.205 --> 02:47.917
I remember he had one son in the ground
and one son trying to be a cop.

02:49.169 --> 02:50.461
You think Stiles' kid?

02:50.545 --> 02:53.506
I don't know, but the tension
between him and OG felt personal.

02:53.590 --> 02:56.342
We need to know more about that
and his issues with his wife.

02:56.426 --> 02:57.468
Right.

03:05.268 --> 03:07.061
Goddamn it.

03:19.240 --> 03:20.450
Fuck.

03:21.784 --> 03:26.289
-Hold on. Slow down. What happened?
-Isaiah. He literally just walked out.

03:26.372 --> 03:29.375
-Missed the end of Noah's game.
-Candace, I'm sorry.

03:29.459 --> 03:31.044
I covered for him with Noah,

03:31.127 --> 03:33.504
but I am so sick and tired
of covering for him, you know?

03:33.588 --> 03:36.090
It's like every time I think
things are getting better,

03:36.174 --> 03:38.426
he gets distracted by something again.

03:39.886 --> 03:42.680
-Uh, Candace, I gotta call you back.
-Bye.

03:51.314 --> 03:53.608
-Hello.
-Hey, baby. It's me.

03:54.150 --> 03:56.069
-Is everything okay?
-Yeah.

03:56.152 --> 03:58.363
How you feeling?

03:58.947 --> 04:03.159
Can't keep anything down this morning.
I guess there's more than one reason why.

04:05.828 --> 04:08.539
That friend that you introduced me to,
Candace Stiles?

04:08.623 --> 04:11.459
-Yeah, I was just talking to her.
-Let me guess. She's mad at her husband?

04:11.542 --> 04:14.837
I dropped some sneakers off
at Noah Stiles' AAU game this morning.

04:15.922 --> 04:17.257
Are you sure that was smart?

04:17.340 --> 04:19.550
I need him off balance.
That's where you come in, baby.

04:19.634 --> 04:21.511
I've seen them twice now,

04:21.594 --> 04:24.180
and their relationship
is on an active fault line.

04:24.264 --> 04:25.932
I need you to get shit shaking.

04:29.435 --> 04:32.146
Babe, Candace is a real friend, and…

04:34.023 --> 04:36.067
I told you,
I don't wanna be involved anymore.

04:36.150 --> 04:37.151
And you won't be.

04:37.235 --> 04:39.487
As soon as you get Candace on lock,

04:39.570 --> 04:42.949
she'll distract Stiles just long enough
for me to do what I need to do

04:43.032 --> 04:45.034
and come home to you.

04:45.118 --> 04:46.911
I'll talk to you tomorrow, alright?
I love you.

05:04.554 --> 05:07.598
-Hey.
-Hey, Candace. Sorry about that.

05:07.682 --> 05:09.976
Do you wanna have lunch tomorrow?

05:10.059 --> 05:12.228
You can talk to me
all about you and Isaiah.

05:12.312 --> 05:15.481
Oh, girl, that's just what I need.

05:19.402 --> 05:20.570
How did Noah do?

05:20.653 --> 05:22.530
Uh… won the game.

05:22.613 --> 05:24.115
What the hell is this?

05:25.992 --> 05:27.243
Yo.

05:27.869 --> 05:30.413
We've got cases piling up,
and you're doing criminal vision boards?

05:30.496 --> 05:33.833
Coltrane Wilder showed up
at Noah's game today,

05:33.916 --> 05:35.710
giving away sneakers.

05:35.793 --> 05:39.297
Cruz, hey, he's taunting me.
Making this shit personal.

05:39.380 --> 05:41.674
These guys made it personal
a long fucking time ago, carnal.

05:41.758 --> 05:44.177
And maybe Coltrane Wilder
is working with them.

05:45.511 --> 05:49.223
Or maybe his morning plans
had nothing to do with you.

05:49.807 --> 05:53.561
"Coltrane Wilder,
CEO of realty company Wilder Holdings,

05:53.644 --> 05:56.105
gifts AAU teams new sneakers."

05:56.189 --> 05:58.232
-Third year in a row.
-It's a fucking… It's a facade.

05:58.316 --> 05:59.484
That's from last year.

05:59.567 --> 06:02.487
This nigga think he Nino Brown
on fucking Thanksgiving.

06:02.570 --> 06:05.865
We still have no hard evidence
connecting Wilder to any crime.

06:06.449 --> 06:09.744
The watch complaint was pulled.
The jewelry heist case is closed.

06:09.827 --> 06:10.912
And Sealey shut us down.

06:11.662 --> 06:13.539
Don't you think it's time to let this go?

06:14.749 --> 06:16.376
He killed Manny Shaw, Cruz.

06:17.126 --> 06:18.461
I know it.

06:18.544 --> 06:20.338
Where's the proof, compa?

06:20.421 --> 06:23.424
Lieutenant, I got a hit on that glass
you brought me the other day.

06:24.008 --> 06:25.343
You stole a glass from the gala?

06:25.426 --> 06:27.929
-I didn't steal it.
-What am I saying? Of course you did.

06:28.012 --> 06:30.139
How much did you pay Yamaguchi
to be here on a Saturday?

06:30.223 --> 06:31.974
Don't worry about that.
What you got for me?

06:32.058 --> 06:34.268
So I compared that glass DNA
to the detonator DNA

06:34.352 --> 06:37.063
from the downtown jewelry heist. No dice.

06:37.146 --> 06:39.774
-But you said you got a hit.
-Two, actually.

06:39.857 --> 06:41.651
Because of your generosity, Stiles,

06:41.734 --> 06:43.820
I reached out
to a forensic genealogist contact

06:43.903 --> 06:47.031
just in case our detonator DNA
matched anyone in our system.

06:47.115 --> 06:51.119
Now, it didn't get an exact match,
but whoever handled that detonator

06:51.202 --> 06:54.956
has a paternal DNA link
with a Donald "Big Crank" Davis

06:55.039 --> 06:56.416
as well as a Darren Stroman.

06:56.499 --> 06:59.377
Davis is doing life
for aggravated manslaughter.

06:59.460 --> 07:01.212
Stroman did some time in Lancaster.

07:01.295 --> 07:05.258
Could be a son, grandson,
nephew, grandnephew.

07:06.592 --> 07:10.513
Stiles, stop by anytime, man.
I'm saving up for a motorcycle.

07:10.596 --> 07:12.515
-I'm your sugar daddy and shit.
-Yeah.

07:12.598 --> 07:14.267
-Cruz.
-Guchi.

07:14.976 --> 07:17.103
Davis. Davis, like Deon Davis.

07:17.186 --> 07:20.022
And Darren fucking Stro, Stroman,

07:20.106 --> 07:23.401
who Coltrane brought
to my son's basketball game today.

07:24.277 --> 07:25.611
Cruz, hey.

07:25.695 --> 07:28.739
I told you. Those Persians
didn't do the jewelry store heist.

07:28.823 --> 07:30.158
Davis is military.

07:30.241 --> 07:32.368
All we have to do now
is just request a DNA match.

07:32.452 --> 07:35.788
Department of Defense gives it to us.
We get the task force back together.

07:35.872 --> 07:38.499
If you got the glass a different way
and tested the DNA, sure.

07:38.583 --> 07:41.377
And you paid Guchi here to do the test!

07:41.461 --> 07:44.380
-None of this is admissible, Stiles.
-Wilder's guys don't know that, Cruz.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.215
-Isaiah.
-Okay, okay, okay, okay.

07:46.299 --> 07:49.635
Viggiano and Harper said that
Stroman has two little girls, right?

07:49.719 --> 07:50.928
Okay.

07:51.554 --> 07:53.181
I'm gonna get him to talk.

08:01.230 --> 08:03.191
You a hard man to find, Darren Stroman.

08:05.151 --> 08:07.820
We had to call your mama's house
to get you to come down here.

08:08.863 --> 08:09.739
Hey, you hungry?

08:10.323 --> 08:11.199
Huh?

08:12.325 --> 08:13.910
What you know about Jim Dandy?

08:15.995 --> 08:18.122
See, I'm a dark meat man myself.

08:18.623 --> 08:20.458
Mm-hmm. Oh, you want a wing?

08:22.001 --> 08:23.628
Strawberry soda?

08:26.631 --> 08:29.133
Fuck it. More for me.

08:30.468 --> 08:31.886
Oh, man.

08:32.428 --> 08:33.262
Mm!

08:35.264 --> 08:36.349
Mm-hmm.

08:38.893 --> 08:41.729
Bro, where was you at on Halloween night?

08:41.812 --> 08:42.855
Mm?

08:43.648 --> 08:45.608
Because I got a robbery
up in Beverly Hills

08:45.691 --> 08:47.693
with your crew's name written all over it.

08:49.237 --> 08:52.281
What about Diamond District?
Been there lately?

08:52.365 --> 08:55.159
'Cause I got you and three other niggas
hitting a series of stores.

08:55.243 --> 08:56.577
Blowing up walls.

08:56.661 --> 08:58.829
And I bet dollars to doughnuts

08:59.664 --> 09:03.000
your baby, Uncle Deon,
was the explosives man.

09:03.084 --> 09:05.378
Y'all dropped two bodies there.

09:05.461 --> 09:10.841
We found some unalive Persians
covered in diamonds.

09:10.925 --> 09:12.927
Four more bodies.

09:13.010 --> 09:15.304
I got good news, and I got bad news.

09:15.388 --> 09:16.806
Bad news,

09:18.015 --> 09:21.477
I got a match for your DNA
from the jewelry store's heist downtown.

09:23.104 --> 09:23.938
Mm-hmm.

09:24.522 --> 09:26.482
You and your whole crew, nigga.

09:29.277 --> 09:30.778
Six bodies.

09:30.861 --> 09:33.281
All in the commission
of multiple felonies.

09:33.364 --> 09:36.284
I've been thinking about a way
to get y'all the federal death penalty.

09:36.367 --> 09:38.953
I've been up at night, dawg.
My wife like, "Come to bed."

09:39.036 --> 09:42.164
I'm like, "How the fuck
do I put these Scooby-Doo niggas away?"

09:43.457 --> 09:45.167
I got it.

09:46.043 --> 09:47.837
Emmanuel Shaw.

09:47.920 --> 09:49.964
That's my former trainee right there.

09:50.047 --> 09:54.802
Shot and killed in pursuit
of your punk-ass crew two years ago.

09:55.761 --> 09:56.721
Tsk.

09:59.515 --> 10:00.558
All right.

10:06.105 --> 10:08.482
You got those two little girls at home.

10:09.859 --> 10:11.527
And they love they daddy.

10:12.153 --> 10:14.989
How will you and your wife
explain to Tiana and Leyla

10:15.072 --> 10:17.658
that you're never coming home?

10:18.284 --> 10:20.661
Oh, wait, no.
I had that good news, remember?

10:20.745 --> 10:22.955
We ain't even after you, man.

10:23.039 --> 10:25.166
You give me Coltrane Wilder.

10:25.249 --> 10:27.335
You tell me your next job.

10:27.418 --> 10:29.795
And I swear
I will find a way to get you a walk.

10:29.879 --> 10:32.006
We'll sweep away the six bodies,

10:32.506 --> 10:33.758
and Manny,

10:33.841 --> 10:35.551
right off of your sheet.

10:36.927 --> 10:39.680
Come on, man.
The evidence is piling up, player.

10:39.764 --> 10:41.349
I know you, nigga.

10:43.476 --> 10:45.436
You must not remember me, though.

10:46.937 --> 10:49.065
I played against you in high school.

10:49.148 --> 10:51.400
Middle linebacker, number 56.

10:52.360 --> 10:56.072
You went to Crenshaw, right? Class of '04?

10:56.614 --> 10:58.658
You was the running back.

10:58.741 --> 11:00.368
Kind of nice with it.

11:00.451 --> 11:03.162
However, last game of the season?

11:04.830 --> 11:07.291
I rocked your shit into next week.

11:07.917 --> 11:10.294
Put you in concussion protocol
before the half.

11:16.509 --> 11:17.718
Jim Dandy.

11:25.768 --> 11:29.313
Louisiana Fried Chicken on Manchester
way better than that bullshit.

11:29.980 --> 11:31.148
Oh.

11:31.232 --> 11:35.861
And if that DNA matched me,
I'd be in cuffs already. Come on.

11:36.570 --> 11:39.240
Either arrest me
and let me call my lawyer,

11:39.323 --> 11:42.076
or I'm gonna get up
out of this funky-ass little room.

11:42.159 --> 11:43.494
It stinks in here.

11:44.995 --> 11:48.290
Am I free to go… officer?

11:54.338 --> 11:55.881
I got Ebony back on the team.

11:56.465 --> 11:59.176
-How'd you get her to do that?
-It doesn't matter. She's in.

11:59.260 --> 12:00.386
In-in.

12:00.469 --> 12:02.430
She's friends
with a lady named Candace Stiles.

12:02.513 --> 12:03.889
Candace Stiles' husband…

12:03.973 --> 12:06.642
Is Isaiah Stiles,
your pain-in-the-ass detective?

12:07.226 --> 12:08.185
Bingo.

12:08.269 --> 12:11.605
Wow, I guess it never occurred to me
that Ebony would be foolish enough

12:11.689 --> 12:13.149
to be friends with a cop's wife.

12:13.232 --> 12:15.151
It might be good for us that she is.

12:15.735 --> 12:18.320
Look, we have firsthand knowledge

12:18.404 --> 12:20.990
that their marriage is about
as brittle as a stale cookie.

12:21.073 --> 12:23.367
Ebony gets in her ear,
I know it'll crumble.

12:23.451 --> 12:25.953
That should slow Stiles down.

12:26.036 --> 12:28.956
At least long enough for us
to get your boy's job done.

12:29.832 --> 12:33.961
I see how that can work
if Ebony's in control of the situation.

12:34.044 --> 12:35.755
She's changed.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.631
You sure she's the one in charge?

12:38.507 --> 12:40.092
I have no doubt.

13:02.948 --> 13:04.366
Dr. Candace Stiles?

13:04.950 --> 13:06.285
Ahh.

13:06.368 --> 13:08.037
I am so embarrassed.

13:08.120 --> 13:12.249
My name's Brenda Johnson,
and I missed the Baldwin Hills Cares Gala.

13:12.333 --> 13:15.503
-My daughter was sick.
-Oh, I am sorry to hear that.

13:15.586 --> 13:17.755
Oh, she's better now, thank you.

13:17.838 --> 13:21.258
I intended to give you this at the gala.

13:21.342 --> 13:24.094
A gift for making Malik Jacobson
our guest of honor.

13:24.678 --> 13:26.347
All the ladies thank you.

13:28.724 --> 13:32.102
It's a couple's gift certificate
from Eden's Bliss Spa.

13:32.186 --> 13:34.438
Maybe you and your husband can go.

13:36.232 --> 13:37.733
I wish.

13:37.817 --> 13:40.152
He's a bit of a workaholic.

13:40.236 --> 13:41.487
-Oh.
-Mm-hmm.

13:41.570 --> 13:44.698
But I have a friend on the planning
committee who might enjoy it.

13:44.782 --> 13:48.702
-If they offer prenatal massages?
-Oh, they offer it all.

13:48.786 --> 13:50.621
Who's your friend? Maybe I know her.

13:50.704 --> 13:51.664
Ebony Wilder.

13:52.998 --> 13:54.250
Have you met?

13:54.333 --> 13:56.669
Ebony Wilder.

13:56.752 --> 14:00.965
I don't know her personally, no,
but it sounds like she could use it.

14:01.048 --> 14:02.424
-Mm.
-Oh.

14:02.508 --> 14:05.803
Gosh, will you look at the time.
I have to go pick the kids up from school.

14:05.886 --> 14:08.055
-But it has been a pleasure meeting you.
-Aww.

14:08.681 --> 14:09.515
-Ah!
-Oh.

14:09.598 --> 14:12.268
-I look forward to seeing you again.
-Likewise.

14:12.351 --> 14:13.978
-Brenda, right?
-Uh-huh.

14:58.147 --> 15:00.232
-What the hell?
-Don't play hero.

15:00.316 --> 15:01.817
This ain't about you.

15:01.901 --> 15:03.152
Exit slowly.

15:03.736 --> 15:05.362
-Slowly!
-All right, all right.

15:08.157 --> 15:09.992
Hands up, motherfucker.

15:11.702 --> 15:13.537
Wakey-wakey!

15:13.621 --> 15:17.041
-Get your motherfucking ass on the ground!
-Guns on the ground! Hurry up!

15:17.124 --> 15:19.209
We're here for your product,
not your lives!

15:19.293 --> 15:21.712
Stay smart, follow directions,
and we'll be gone soon!

15:21.795 --> 15:25.299
-Get on the fucking ground now!
-Don't be stupid. Your hands down!

15:25.382 --> 15:27.760
What the fuck you looking at?
Your ass on the ground, now!

15:29.178 --> 15:30.512
-Phones.
-In the bag.

15:30.596 --> 15:32.890
-Phones in the bag.
-Come on, phones!

15:32.973 --> 15:35.309
Phones, phones!
Give me that fucking Android.

15:35.392 --> 15:36.852
I'll say this once.

15:36.936 --> 15:41.565
In 90 minutes, a truck containing
one million single-gram vials of ketamine

15:41.649 --> 15:43.484
will be coming to loading dock number 1.

15:43.567 --> 15:46.278
That truck will be leaving with us!

15:46.362 --> 15:48.447
We're not expecting
any deliveries tonight.

15:52.785 --> 15:54.954
Lie to me once, shame on you.

15:55.871 --> 15:57.122
Lie to me twice…

15:58.248 --> 16:01.585
I use this bullet to bore a hole
straight through your skull.

16:02.336 --> 16:06.256
Right now, I need complete compliance.

16:06.757 --> 16:10.344
If you can do that, I promise
you will make it out of this alive.

16:10.427 --> 16:12.846
Green. Red. Get these people situated.

16:12.930 --> 16:15.432
-Y'all asses up!
-Hurry up before I start shooting!

16:15.516 --> 16:17.518
-Hurry the fuck up!
-To the break room!

16:17.601 --> 16:18.852
-Move it!
-You heard him!

16:18.936 --> 16:20.813
-To the fucking break room!
-Move it!

16:20.896 --> 16:22.982
Put some pep in that motherfucking step!

16:23.065 --> 16:27.027
Slow dancing in this burning house

16:28.487 --> 16:29.655
I don't wanna go nowhere…

16:29.738 --> 16:32.408
You gonna punish me for inviting
my grandfather to my basketball game?

16:37.913 --> 16:40.374
Nobody said anything about punishing you.
Chill out.

16:41.125 --> 16:44.461
It's your game, kid. If you want
your grandfather there, it is what it is.

16:44.545 --> 16:47.631
When there's miles
And miles of distance

16:48.590 --> 16:49.425
Seriously?

16:49.508 --> 16:51.385
Feel your heart is drifting…

16:51.468 --> 16:52.302
Mm-hmm.

16:54.471 --> 16:56.974
You guys finished?
I-- I'll go fill the dishwasher.

16:58.559 --> 17:01.603
Uh, yes. And thank you.

17:02.604 --> 17:04.398
-Thank you, Noah.
-Yeah.

17:04.481 --> 17:05.482
Good man.

17:10.404 --> 17:12.031
You handled that well.

17:12.114 --> 17:14.867
I still don't want
his grimy-ass grandfather

17:14.950 --> 17:17.244
and his gangster disciples
hanging around our son,

17:17.327 --> 17:19.038
but it's not Noah's problem.

17:19.663 --> 17:22.124
He's just a kid.
I'm gonna handle it with Amos.

17:22.833 --> 17:24.877
No, I--
I promise I'm just gonna talk to him.

17:24.960 --> 17:28.088
He just needs to understand
who's appropriate to bring around our son.

17:31.717 --> 17:35.012
I'm sorry I left the game early.
It won't happen again.

17:38.223 --> 17:40.517
You sound a lot like the old Isaiah.

17:41.685 --> 17:43.562
It's nice to know
he's still in there somewhere.

17:45.230 --> 17:46.523
I never left.

17:47.691 --> 17:50.986
Candace, I maybe got distracted,
and I'm sorry for that, but…

17:52.821 --> 17:54.198
But I'm still here.

17:54.281 --> 17:56.492
You are my only choice…

17:56.575 --> 17:57.576
Are you?

17:57.659 --> 18:00.954
And we're both just filling voids…

18:03.582 --> 18:04.708
I miss you.

18:06.668 --> 18:08.378
Shh.

18:08.462 --> 18:10.380
Who you telling, huh? Come here, girl.

18:15.094 --> 18:16.887
-Mm.
-Mm. Mm-hmm.

18:16.970 --> 18:17.846
Mm-hmm.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.139
Yeah, come here.

18:19.890 --> 18:21.308
Noah, go to bed!

18:21.934 --> 18:23.268
Ew!

18:23.352 --> 18:26.230
But that is still debatable…

18:31.110 --> 18:34.738
I miss being able to turn over
and look at you lying next to me.

18:34.822 --> 18:38.033
Well… we could do it
all over again in the morning.

18:38.117 --> 18:39.660
Mm!

18:39.743 --> 18:42.121
-Get some food afterwards.
-Mm-hmm?

18:42.204 --> 18:43.997
Get back to it at night, if you want.

18:46.166 --> 18:47.501
Oh, baby.

18:48.627 --> 18:50.921
-I wish I could, but…
-Mm.

18:51.421 --> 18:53.340
I'm meeting Ebony at her house for lunch.

18:55.926 --> 18:57.719
I hope you're not mad.

18:59.221 --> 19:00.472
It's all good.

19:29.209 --> 19:31.628
-Truck's almost here.
-No doubt.

19:34.214 --> 19:35.424
Incoming.

19:50.355 --> 19:53.775
Wanna make it home to Kyle, James,
and that lovely wife of yours, Nancy,

19:53.859 --> 19:55.736
I suggest you listen to my boy.

19:56.236 --> 19:57.821
Your load is ours, understand?

19:58.864 --> 19:59.698
Fuck that truck.

20:00.699 --> 20:01.909
Get the magic wand.

20:06.455 --> 20:07.998
Tracker one.

20:10.626 --> 20:11.460
Tracker two.

20:13.086 --> 20:15.797
Workers are secure.
Ready to roll when you are.

20:15.881 --> 20:18.926
Listen the fuck up.
Tell them to open the gate.

20:19.009 --> 20:22.262
You do some dumb shit, it's gonna be
the last thing you fucking do. Feel me?

20:24.223 --> 20:26.475
-Open the gate.
-Copy.

20:31.230 --> 20:34.650
-Last tracker.
-Time to roll out. Let's go.

20:47.579 --> 20:50.874
-We killed that shit, cuh!
-Indeed, we fucking did.

20:50.958 --> 20:54.378
Stro, Choi, you commanded this space.

20:54.461 --> 20:58.257
And you, you held that shit the fuck down.

20:58.340 --> 21:01.343
You kept the workers in check,
and stood on business. I see you.

21:01.426 --> 21:03.804
To us.

21:03.887 --> 21:06.515
Our fourth and final job.

21:06.598 --> 21:11.478
We came out alive, on top,
and about to make fucking millions.

21:12.437 --> 21:13.814
Happy holidays, my niggas.

21:26.702 --> 21:30.163
Jimmy. Hey, you know
the silver alert from last night?

21:30.247 --> 21:33.375
My guys created a distraction again.

21:33.458 --> 21:36.253
-What the hell are you doing here?
-I'm working this case.

21:36.336 --> 21:38.505
First of all, you haven't
been assigned to this case.

21:38.588 --> 21:41.341
Second, you didn't
even have the courtesy to call me?

21:41.925 --> 21:45.220
I'm not about to get fucked by the brass
'cause you listened to a scanner

21:45.304 --> 21:47.806
and acted off a hunch. Cruz!

21:50.267 --> 21:52.227
I thought you'd at least know better.

21:52.728 --> 21:55.355
-What did you want me to do?
-The two of you are done here.

21:55.439 --> 21:59.818
Hold up. You send me home right now,
you flood all of Southern California,

21:59.901 --> 22:01.320
possibly Nevada and Arizona,

22:01.403 --> 22:04.948
with a million grams
of pharmaceutical-grade ketamine, Jimmy.

22:05.032 --> 22:07.159
You know that's the primary precursor
to tusi, right?

22:07.242 --> 22:10.996
That's right, Isaiah.
One million grams of ketamine.

22:11.538 --> 22:15.459
The DEA, FBI, and about 100 motherfuckers
in different windbreakers

22:15.542 --> 22:17.377
are about to descend on this warehouse.

22:17.461 --> 22:20.213
And the last thing I need
is you telling any of them

22:20.297 --> 22:23.300
that you think there are only
four possible suspects

22:23.383 --> 22:25.302
in the whole goddamn Southland.

22:25.385 --> 22:27.429
-Because they--
-Not another word.

22:29.431 --> 22:30.682
All right, shit.

22:32.517 --> 22:33.685
Jesus.

22:35.395 --> 22:37.439
Everything under control, Captain?

22:38.023 --> 22:40.484
Yeah. Yeah.

22:40.567 --> 22:44.404
Your boy's good, but not good enough
to be pulling this shit.

22:55.332 --> 22:57.542
Mm.

22:57.626 --> 23:01.046
I think we found the secret cure
for morning sickness.

23:01.129 --> 23:03.382
I wish I knew it was that easy.

23:04.341 --> 23:06.968
I think it's 'cause it's over.

23:07.052 --> 23:08.637
And you're home with me.

23:08.720 --> 23:12.474
I'm all yours from here on out.
No more jobs.

23:13.475 --> 23:15.227
What about Charlie and the guys?

23:15.310 --> 23:19.481
Only reason for Charlie to call me
moving forward is to ask about you.

23:19.564 --> 23:20.732
Or see our child.

23:21.942 --> 23:23.276
The guys will be fine.

23:23.360 --> 23:25.404
About to clear
a little over two million each.

23:25.487 --> 23:27.114
I think they'll be okay when I…

23:28.281 --> 23:30.158
When I tell them I'm done.

23:30.909 --> 23:32.119
I'm really done.

23:35.163 --> 23:37.874
Destination is forever

23:37.958 --> 23:40.210
The sky is just the beginning

23:40.293 --> 23:41.795
I'm really done.

23:42.504 --> 23:43.588
Ooh, we'll be…

23:46.675 --> 23:48.009
-Yes?
-Change of plans.

23:48.093 --> 23:49.344
I'm not taking the load.

23:50.095 --> 23:52.389
The fuck you're not.
We have a deal, Andrei.

23:53.098 --> 23:55.100
And now I'm saying we don't.

23:56.435 --> 23:57.936
You came to me.

23:58.019 --> 24:01.314
Asked for a risky job to be done.
My crew executed it flawlessly.

24:01.398 --> 24:04.067
Now you wanna back out?
No, that's not how this works.

24:04.151 --> 24:05.235
Shh, shh.

24:05.318 --> 24:06.778
Shh.

24:08.780 --> 24:10.866
You talk too much for a woman.

24:12.242 --> 24:16.329
You know who I am,
who my family is, what we do.

24:16.413 --> 24:22.085
You know we take women like you,
and we make them disappear.

24:22.878 --> 24:25.422
Right… Charlotte?

24:27.841 --> 24:29.843
There's no need for threats.

24:29.926 --> 24:32.554
I respect you and your family.

24:33.054 --> 24:34.306
Now, let's back up.

24:34.890 --> 24:37.434
I can assure safe delivery--

24:39.352 --> 24:41.313
Fuck me.

24:57.954 --> 24:59.080
Coltrane.

24:59.706 --> 25:02.459
We need to talk. Now.

25:02.542 --> 25:06.004
The load is dead.
For whatever reason, buyer's backed out.

25:06.087 --> 25:07.464
-Are you serious?
-Backed out?

25:07.547 --> 25:09.007
They're not paying us for the load.

25:09.090 --> 25:11.009
What they think
we finna do with this shit?

25:11.092 --> 25:14.262
Fuck that. Them niggas just played us.
I ain't going out like that, cuh.

25:14.346 --> 25:18.016
-They gotta run us their nine M's.
-We don't even know the buyer.

25:18.099 --> 25:20.018
Fuck it. Let's move them shits ourselves.

25:20.101 --> 25:22.812
Nah, you talking crazy, Unc.
That's not our lane.

25:22.896 --> 25:25.982
What lane we in right now then?
Must be the lane for suckers.

25:26.066 --> 25:28.944
We live off the land, y'all.
Eat what we kill.

25:29.027 --> 25:32.489
We slaughtered the whole fucking farm,
and now you telling us we can't feast?

25:32.572 --> 25:35.867
I paid what I owe. The fourth job.
Alright? Cashing it out isn't up to me.

25:35.951 --> 25:38.078
The fuck you good for then, nigga?

25:38.161 --> 25:40.247
What happens after a job
is out of my control.

25:40.330 --> 25:42.040
And even if I wanted to…

25:44.292 --> 25:45.418
This was it for me. I'm done.

25:45.502 --> 25:47.754
-What you talking about?
-I'm done!

25:48.922 --> 25:51.049
This is my last run. Payday or no payday.

25:51.132 --> 25:53.927
That's it for me.
I gotta look out for my family.

25:54.594 --> 25:56.846
All right? My wife needs me. I need me.

25:56.930 --> 25:59.933
The fuck kind of new age
life coach kombucha bullshit is that?

26:00.016 --> 26:02.852
Talking about you need you!
We need this money, nigga.

26:02.936 --> 26:06.231
I kept my word to you.
I kept my fucking word.

26:06.314 --> 26:08.358
Now I gotta make
my next move be my best move.

26:08.441 --> 26:10.360
I have to keep my word to Ebony.

26:10.443 --> 26:11.361
And to myself.

26:18.368 --> 26:20.912
I'll be in contact
with instructions on dumping the load.

26:23.415 --> 26:25.000
What the fuck, cuh?!

26:25.083 --> 26:26.084
Hey!

26:27.419 --> 26:29.963
You better talk to your mans, nephew.
Get us our fucking paper.

26:30.046 --> 26:33.216
I don't care if he is feeling
some kind of way. I need my M!

26:33.300 --> 26:35.093
Chill, D. He's done.

26:35.176 --> 26:37.220
Let him go.
We gotta figure out another score.

26:37.304 --> 26:39.764
I'll move these bitches
my goddamn self if I have to.

26:39.848 --> 26:41.766
Hey, check your temperature, nigga.

26:41.850 --> 26:45.103
You already know I can't let you do that.
Take a fucking breath.

26:45.186 --> 26:47.188
Cool him out, Choi.
I'm gonna be right back.

26:48.440 --> 26:51.318
-Yo, you wildin', man.
-Man, get the fuck off me.

26:53.903 --> 26:54.904
'Trane!

26:57.782 --> 27:01.202
Hey, yo, what the fuck?
That's a lot to drop on us at once.

27:01.286 --> 27:03.371
-No payday, and you fucking leaving?
-Hey.

27:04.039 --> 27:07.042
Might be a good time
for you to get out too, Stro.

27:07.125 --> 27:08.710
We got a bigger problem.

27:08.793 --> 27:12.547
My guy says the buyer who backed out
is acting kind of wild.

27:12.631 --> 27:14.883
He thinks he's up to something.
Doesn't know what.

27:15.550 --> 27:17.427
Buyer needs to be found and followed.

27:17.510 --> 27:20.847
-So what's up? We gonna chip him?
-No, just get some intel.

27:20.930 --> 27:23.808
-Tail him, see what we see.
-All right, I'll tell Deon and Choi.

27:23.892 --> 27:28.480
No, no. Deon needs to sit this out.
Cool his head a little bit.

27:29.064 --> 27:32.525
Get Choi involved
after Deon goes home, all right?

27:32.609 --> 27:33.943
Three of us can handle this.

27:35.403 --> 27:38.198
Man, you out? For real?

27:40.909 --> 27:42.160
I am, bro.

27:45.372 --> 27:46.539
I have to.

27:50.543 --> 27:51.419
Love you, man.

27:53.546 --> 27:54.798
I love you too.

28:18.738 --> 28:19.572
Hey, baby.

28:21.533 --> 28:22.826
Pow.

28:22.909 --> 28:25.954
What is-- What is this? Another one?

28:26.037 --> 28:27.664
Isaiah…

28:29.374 --> 28:31.710
-Are you serious?
-For leaving the game early.

28:33.420 --> 28:35.422
Thank you, baby.

28:35.505 --> 28:37.382
-It's good.
-Yeah, it's good.

28:37.465 --> 28:39.467
It's good, babe.

28:39.551 --> 28:42.095
-Help me put it on.
-Yeah, I got you. Get the hair for me.

28:42.178 --> 28:44.556
Ah.

28:44.639 --> 28:47.183
-Here.
-Mm-hmm. Hold up. Let me get it like that.

28:47.267 --> 28:48.810
-Ooh.
-Yeah, yeah, hold on.

28:48.893 --> 28:51.938
-There it is.
-Look. It matches my bracelet.

28:52.021 --> 28:54.441
Oh, what am I gonna do with you?

28:54.524 --> 28:57.902
We can go upstairs 'cause I got
a few ideas of what you can do to me.

28:57.986 --> 28:59.988
Mm.

29:01.156 --> 29:05.493
I wish I could take you down right now,
but my Uber's here.

29:05.577 --> 29:07.412
-Take me to Ebony's.
-Oh, no, babe.

29:07.495 --> 29:11.291
Yeah, I know.
But I'm having wine for lunch.

29:11.833 --> 29:13.585
You know what that does to me.

29:13.668 --> 29:17.589
So, how about you pick me up later
and we can explore what you have in mind.

29:17.672 --> 29:18.757
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

29:18.840 --> 29:20.049
Mm.

29:20.675 --> 29:21.509
One more time.

29:21.593 --> 29:22.719
-Mm.
-Mm.

29:23.970 --> 29:26.347
-See you later, babe.
-All right, all right, hold on, hold on.

29:26.431 --> 29:28.057
Babe!

29:38.485 --> 29:41.154
-Hey, happy birthday, Big Mama.
-Hey!

29:41.237 --> 29:44.199
-How's my grandbaby?
-Good, come in.

29:44.282 --> 29:47.535
-Don't get jealous, Regina.
-Ain't nobody jealous, Mama.

29:47.619 --> 29:49.037
Her son know who his Mama is.

29:49.120 --> 29:50.413
-How you doing, Mama?
-Good.

29:50.497 --> 29:52.707
-Good to see you. Come in.
-Good to see you too.

29:52.791 --> 29:55.210
So Jamise and the girls,
they at her mama's crib.

29:55.293 --> 29:58.588
-They be here in a little bit.
-Okay, they can wait. I'm here to see you.

29:59.589 --> 30:01.674
-You okay, baby?
-Yeah, I'm great.

30:01.758 --> 30:06.387
-Why? I got something on my face?
-No, no, you look fine. I just…

30:07.263 --> 30:09.641
I had a dream last night.

30:10.517 --> 30:13.394
And you were crying your little eyes out.

30:15.355 --> 30:17.315
You ain't gotta worry about that.

30:17.398 --> 30:19.776
Shit, I ain't cried since…

30:20.735 --> 30:21.611
Yo.

30:21.694 --> 30:25.156
Since you whupped Deon's ass for breaking
your little mini-sculpture of Black Jesus.

30:25.240 --> 30:26.074
You remember that?

30:26.157 --> 30:30.411
It was a figurine, Darren, that I got
on my one trip to the Bahamas.

30:30.495 --> 30:34.082
My fault, Big Mama.
But for real. You beat his ass so bad.

30:34.165 --> 30:36.918
And I was in the corner crying
like a baby, thinking I was next.

30:38.002 --> 30:40.088
Where is Deon? Is he coming?

30:40.171 --> 30:42.423
Big Mama, you know that nigga always--

30:43.049 --> 30:43.967
Excuse me.

30:44.050 --> 30:47.387
You know Deon's always gonna be late,
but he be here in a second, I promise.

30:47.470 --> 30:49.264
Okay.

30:49.347 --> 30:50.181
Oh!

30:50.265 --> 30:51.099
Come on.

30:51.182 --> 30:54.644
Lord, there's Deon! I just said his name.

30:54.727 --> 30:57.647
Look at my baby's babies coming.

30:57.730 --> 30:59.607
-Ooh!
-What's up, Mama?

30:59.691 --> 31:00.859
Ooh!

31:01.651 --> 31:02.610
Come here, cuz.

31:02.694 --> 31:05.029
How you doing, girl? Good to see you.

31:06.072 --> 31:07.991
What up, man? Give me a hug.

31:08.074 --> 31:10.827
-Happy C-Day, Mama.
-Thank you, baby.

31:10.910 --> 31:12.829
-Thank you!
-Mwah! Yeah!

31:12.912 --> 31:16.624
So good to see y'all.
Hi, honey. How you doing?

31:16.708 --> 31:18.334
Thank you. Look!

31:18.418 --> 31:20.628
-I like your cardigan.
-I hate you.

31:20.712 --> 31:22.422
Looking all spiffy.

31:24.632 --> 31:26.217
You know, you were right.

31:26.301 --> 31:30.013
I told Coltrane about the baby,
and he was so excited.

31:30.096 --> 31:33.975
-He had to contain himself at the gala.
-Aww, yeah!

31:34.058 --> 31:38.271
Speaking of, I heard you left with Malik.

31:39.188 --> 31:40.231
Oh my God.

31:40.315 --> 31:43.276
Is everyone talking
about me getting in his car?

31:43.359 --> 31:47.155
If it's just an innocent ride home,
it shouldn't be a problem, right?

31:47.238 --> 31:50.366
Until it does become a problem. Fuck.

31:50.450 --> 31:52.035
Mm!

31:52.118 --> 31:55.038
Malik and I,
we briefly dated back in college.

31:55.121 --> 31:57.040
-Oh.
-Before Isaiah, of course.

31:57.916 --> 32:00.793
On paper, Malik was…

32:00.877 --> 32:04.464
He looked like the more obvious choice,
especially to my parents.

32:04.547 --> 32:06.925
Who in their twenties
cares about what looks good on paper?

32:07.008 --> 32:08.509
Mm.

32:08.593 --> 32:13.514
Isaiah and I just… I don't know.
He just had something better to offer.

32:14.766 --> 32:16.434
You like them thugs, huh?

32:18.394 --> 32:20.563
Noah aside,
have you ever genuinely considered

32:20.647 --> 32:24.025
what life would be like
had you chosen Malik over Isaiah?

32:25.151 --> 32:27.070
You better answer right, girl.

32:27.153 --> 32:30.406
Between us, since the separation, I have.

32:30.490 --> 32:31.324
Mm.

32:32.909 --> 32:35.244
-What the fuck?
-Like today, we're good.

32:35.328 --> 32:39.624
And when things
are good between us, oh, girl.

32:39.707 --> 32:41.000
Mm!

32:42.627 --> 32:44.170
But when they're bad…

32:46.339 --> 32:48.341
He just makes me feel…

32:50.301 --> 32:51.344
Yeah.

32:52.011 --> 32:53.137
I have thought.

32:53.846 --> 32:57.058
I do think… maybe…

32:57.558 --> 32:59.686
what if I made the wrong decision?

32:59.769 --> 33:04.607
There might be a reason why the universe
has put Malik back in your life now.

33:05.441 --> 33:07.402
Noah's not a little kid anymore.

33:07.485 --> 33:09.570
You might wanna use your intuition.

33:09.654 --> 33:11.447
Explore your options.

33:11.948 --> 33:15.118
Think about what you want
for the rest of your life.

33:16.661 --> 33:18.746
I think you owe it to yourself.

33:19.497 --> 33:21.082
Yeah, fuck you too, Ebony.

33:22.250 --> 33:25.461
-Oh, these pancakes hitting.
-Yeah.

33:25.545 --> 33:28.131
It's fucked up you had Big Mama
make 'em on her birthday.

33:29.257 --> 33:30.633
Shut up and pass the syrup.

33:32.885 --> 33:34.679
-Thank you.
-Mm.

33:36.222 --> 33:38.558
Yo, you talk to 'Trane yet about the load?

33:38.641 --> 33:41.853
You know he'd be listening to you
when it's just the two of y'all.

33:41.936 --> 33:45.314
His mind is made up, all right?
So just dead that thought.

33:45.815 --> 33:48.317
Look, them vials is locked away
with the key in Choi's pocket.

33:48.401 --> 33:50.653
'Trane will decide
what he wants to do when he's ready.

33:50.737 --> 33:52.739
He's gonna dump 'em
in the middle of nowhere.

33:52.822 --> 33:55.616
And then we assed out $9 million.

33:55.700 --> 33:58.161
I mean, he ain't even gonna try.

34:02.040 --> 34:03.583
Everybody…

34:03.666 --> 34:05.460
Aah! Shit!

34:06.669 --> 34:07.628
Get your ass up.

34:07.712 --> 34:09.255
Yeah!

34:10.089 --> 34:13.593
Hey! Get the footwork. What?

34:13.676 --> 34:14.802
Hey! What?

34:14.886 --> 34:17.388
Hey! Get 'em, Ma! Hey!

34:17.472 --> 34:18.473
Get 'em!

34:19.015 --> 34:20.683
Wait, wait.

34:21.893 --> 34:23.728
Yo, I gotta take this, cuh.

34:24.312 --> 34:27.565
Yo. All right, hold on.
Hey, stay off my plate.

34:28.149 --> 34:30.443
I know how many sausages I got too.

34:30.526 --> 34:33.863
Come on.

34:33.946 --> 34:36.407
Every watch I got cost a brick

34:36.491 --> 34:38.367
Everybody with me wearing Rick, yeah

34:38.451 --> 34:40.453
Everytime she see me
She get… and I slip…

34:45.917 --> 34:48.461
Yeah, if you want them,
you gotta take them all.

34:49.337 --> 34:51.380
What? Nah, I need $10 a gram, cuh.

34:51.464 --> 34:54.634
This the type of shit doctors prescribe
to white niggas at Burning Man.

34:54.717 --> 34:57.970
Not that animal-grade garbage
they sling downtown, you feel me?

34:58.971 --> 35:02.183
All right, hey,
make sure his paper's straight.

35:03.184 --> 35:04.560
You know where I'll be.

35:12.485 --> 35:13.694
Hey, boy.

35:15.947 --> 35:17.782
That's not funny.

35:20.660 --> 35:22.578
-Hey, Ma, I'll be right back.
-Okay.

35:25.414 --> 35:26.415
Hey, Big Mama.

35:26.499 --> 35:29.001
-I gotta step out for a second.
-Right now?

35:29.085 --> 35:31.796
-I know. I'm so, so, so sorry.
-I actually gotta head out too, Ma.

35:31.879 --> 35:32.880
Wait, where?

35:34.674 --> 35:37.176
You two going somewhere together?

35:39.679 --> 35:43.641
Never mind. I know better
than to ask you two what you're doing.

35:43.724 --> 35:46.477
I promise I'll be right back, okay?
I know it's your special day.

35:46.561 --> 35:48.354
-Yeah, no doubt, Ma.
-I love you.

35:49.230 --> 35:50.940
Love you too, baby.

35:53.276 --> 35:56.654
Free from all this misery…

35:56.737 --> 35:59.448
Hey, nigga. You better be right back, D.

35:59.532 --> 36:01.868
Hey, chill, nephew. Trust me.

36:03.077 --> 36:04.412
Stu-- Fuck me.

36:09.542 --> 36:12.962
I just don't know
which version of Isaiah I'm gonna get.

36:13.045 --> 36:14.881
The loving, wonderful man I met,

36:14.964 --> 36:19.844
or this cold, distant,
hyper-focused ghost.

36:19.927 --> 36:22.597
What's he so focused on
if he's not focused on you?

36:22.680 --> 36:25.933
-Well, he was focused on me last night.
-Oh.

36:28.603 --> 36:30.855
But then I woke up!

36:30.938 --> 36:34.734
He's out in the guesthouse,
listening to the police scanner.

36:34.817 --> 36:37.361
-Like, that's weird.
-Yeah, that's weird.

36:38.946 --> 36:41.908
No, I'm not supposed
to talk about his cases.

36:44.202 --> 36:46.120
Oh, I can keep a secret.

36:49.665 --> 36:51.167
A couple years ago,

36:51.834 --> 36:54.045
he had this detective trainee
named Manny Shaw.

36:54.795 --> 36:56.047
We all got to know him.

36:56.130 --> 36:59.592
He had meals at our house,
hung out with Noah.

37:00.176 --> 37:01.886
He was a really great kid.

37:02.470 --> 37:06.515
He and Isaiah responded to a robbery,
and Manny was shot and killed.

37:07.642 --> 37:09.101
Isaiah took it so hard.

37:10.853 --> 37:12.271
He blamed himself.

37:15.858 --> 37:19.695
I thought that they caught
the man who did it.

37:19.779 --> 37:25.534
But Isaiah just told me that he thinks
that the man he's chasing now

37:25.618 --> 37:28.371
is the one who really killed Manny.

37:28.871 --> 37:30.122
Well…

37:30.206 --> 37:31.916
Is that what you think?

37:31.999 --> 37:34.043
I don't know what to think.

37:34.126 --> 37:36.045
I just want my husband back.

37:39.966 --> 37:41.342
How are you with massages?

37:41.425 --> 37:43.511
-I love them.
-Mm!

37:46.806 --> 37:48.391
Wanna go?

37:51.852 --> 37:54.939
"Eden's Bliss Spa." Where'd you get this?

37:55.022 --> 37:57.733
A really nice lady
hand-delivered it to my house.

37:58.484 --> 38:02.113
-Uh… Brenda Johnson?
-Yeah, I think I know her.

38:02.196 --> 38:03.823
Tall, light eyes, fake Birkin.

38:03.906 --> 38:05.992
Oh!

38:06.075 --> 38:06.909
Yes.

38:06.993 --> 38:08.119
Yeah.

38:08.202 --> 38:11.163
But I mentioned your name,
and she said she didn't know you.

38:12.081 --> 38:13.082
Oh.

38:13.165 --> 38:14.375
I don't know.

38:14.458 --> 38:16.043
Oh.

38:16.127 --> 38:18.713
Sorry, I told him to text me
when he got here.

38:18.796 --> 38:20.089
No, that's okay.

38:26.721 --> 38:29.140
Isaiah. Candace will be right out.

38:29.223 --> 38:32.268
Hey, Ebony, good to see you.
Mind if I use your bathroom?

38:32.351 --> 38:34.937
-Yeah, it's just that way.
-Thank you.

38:40.192 --> 38:41.402
Shit.

38:49.118 --> 38:50.745
Oh my God.

39:54.016 --> 39:56.185
Yo.

39:58.354 --> 40:00.189
My bad, 'Trane, for coming up here,

40:00.272 --> 40:02.733
but I wanted to hear it
from the horse's mouth.

40:02.817 --> 40:04.110
That load really a wrap?

40:04.193 --> 40:07.530
It don't make sense for us to do
all that work just to let it go to waste.

40:07.613 --> 40:09.865
I got connects. I can flip this shit, cuh.

40:09.949 --> 40:12.201
All I need you to do is say the word.

40:15.454 --> 40:20.126
The money's staring us right in the face.
I-- I got responsibilities to handle, cuh.

40:20.209 --> 40:24.672
Everybody got responsibilities, Deon.
You, Stro, Choi, me.

40:24.755 --> 40:26.632
I got mouths to feed at home too.

40:28.676 --> 40:31.178
Mouths at home? What, Ebony pregnant?

40:33.264 --> 40:36.267
Congratulations, homey.
I didn't know y'all was expecting.

40:36.350 --> 40:39.979
Hey. And look, as a father-to-be,

40:40.062 --> 40:42.565
don't you wanna set your kids up
for the rest of their life?

40:42.648 --> 40:45.776
Ain't that what you always kicking to us?
That generational wealth shit?

40:46.360 --> 40:50.322
I was banking on this last job
to get my family straight, man.

40:55.161 --> 40:56.537
You're right, Deon.

40:56.620 --> 40:59.790
This last one was on me. I mean,
you did the work, but didn't get a reward.

40:59.874 --> 41:01.041
Do me a favor.

41:02.042 --> 41:03.544
Get Rena on the phone.

41:04.753 --> 41:06.130
Get her on the phone.

41:09.049 --> 41:11.635
Where the hell you at?
The kids are doing a talent show.

41:11.719 --> 41:14.680
Hey, baby, hold up.
I got 'Trane here. He wanna speak.

41:16.265 --> 41:17.391
Hey, Rena.

41:17.892 --> 41:20.478
I'm gonna make this quick
so I can send Deon back to you.

41:20.561 --> 41:22.480
Text me your bank's name and their address

41:22.563 --> 41:24.356
plus your bank account
and routing numbers.

41:24.440 --> 41:25.608
In about an hour or so,

41:25.691 --> 41:30.988
$500,000 will be wired to your account
from Wilder Holdings, Incorporated.

41:31.071 --> 41:33.157
-Hold up. What?
-Yes, Rena.

41:33.240 --> 41:34.325
Happy holidays.

41:36.410 --> 41:38.704
Well, oh-- oh my God. Wait.

41:38.787 --> 41:41.916
I-- I don't even know what to say
right now. Thank you, Coltrane.

41:41.999 --> 41:43.334
This gonna change everything.

41:44.001 --> 41:46.504
You don't have to say anything.
You're welcome. All right, now.

41:49.298 --> 41:51.258
Nigga, what the fuck was that?

41:51.342 --> 41:53.177
I don't want your money.

41:53.260 --> 41:55.471
-Then what the fuck do you want, Deon?
-Respect, nigga!

41:55.554 --> 41:59.266
I can't put that kind of cash
in your hot little hands, man.

41:59.350 --> 42:02.937
Plus, if I gave it to you, that puts us
both at risk for the feds to trace.

42:03.020 --> 42:07.107
Giving the money to Rena, right,
for a down payment on a home,

42:07.191 --> 42:08.651
that's kosher.

42:08.734 --> 42:10.402
I'm gonna set you up with properties.

42:10.486 --> 42:13.197
Then I'm gonna have my company
manage them for you,

42:13.280 --> 42:15.866
just like we do with Stro and Choi.
All right?

42:15.950 --> 42:18.744
You'll have steady cash flow,
month after month,

42:18.827 --> 42:20.704
for doing absolutely nothing.

42:23.249 --> 42:26.085
Or… you could've given me that paper,

42:26.168 --> 42:28.796
and I could've flipped it
into an M off top.

42:29.505 --> 42:31.006
You don't trust me.

42:33.133 --> 42:34.927
I trust you to be you.

42:37.054 --> 42:39.723
Now, can I trust that you'll forget
this load exists, man?

42:50.359 --> 42:51.360
You got it.

42:54.697 --> 42:56.073
The load's a wrap.

42:57.032 --> 42:57.950
Okay.

43:09.253 --> 43:11.088
Businessman.

43:29.565 --> 43:31.400
"Brenda Johnson"?

43:31.483 --> 43:33.736
Still calling the same old play, huh?

43:33.819 --> 43:36.238
Have Candace down
to your little front, the spa,

43:36.322 --> 43:38.073
and get her to confide to the masseuse

43:38.157 --> 43:40.743
while one of your girls
goes through her purse in the locker room?

43:40.826 --> 43:43.287
She's a civilian, a mark.

43:43.370 --> 43:45.664
I got her to buy into the spa scam
without breaking a sweat.

43:45.748 --> 43:47.833
How can you waste your time
on someone like that?

43:47.916 --> 43:51.253
It's Candace Stiles.
She trusts me completely.

43:51.337 --> 43:53.339
I have her eating
out of the palm of my hand.

43:53.422 --> 43:54.757
Look at these.

43:54.840 --> 43:56.925
She still has feelings
for her ex from college.

43:57.009 --> 43:58.802
I have her questioning
not only her marriage,

43:58.886 --> 44:00.554
but every life choice she's ever made.

44:00.638 --> 44:02.222
Nice work.

44:02.806 --> 44:05.184
You were able to put aside
your little friendship

44:05.267 --> 44:06.727
for the good of the family.

44:06.810 --> 44:09.021
I will do what needs to be done,

44:09.104 --> 44:11.315
even if it means
hurting someone I care about.

44:11.398 --> 44:13.359
Someone you care about?

44:14.568 --> 44:15.569
Wow.

44:21.075 --> 44:22.826
Congrats on the baby, by the way.

44:27.831 --> 44:30.501
You could've told me
before you told the cop's wife.

44:31.669 --> 44:34.421
At least I knew she'd be happy for me.

44:58.195 --> 44:59.029
Yo!

44:59.697 --> 45:01.532
-What up, cuh?
-What's good?

45:01.615 --> 45:04.410
The nameplate just came in
for your mama's chain.

45:04.493 --> 45:05.369
Piece is hittin'.

45:05.452 --> 45:08.497
-Yo. You got it on you right now?
-Cousin's inside wrapping it up.

45:08.580 --> 45:10.040
I'm gonna need the full amount, D.

45:11.041 --> 45:12.793
Say less, nigga.

45:12.876 --> 45:14.420
Damn!

45:14.962 --> 45:18.757
Horse just come in or something?
Losing streak's over now, huh?

45:19.925 --> 45:23.178
-Let's go get your mama's gift.
-Nah, man. I'm gonna stay here.

45:23.262 --> 45:25.139
I ain't trying to run into no crazy exes.

45:25.222 --> 45:27.266
One in there now.
On God, I seen her pull up.

45:27.349 --> 45:29.935
-You a scary ass motherfucker, cuz.
-Yeah.

45:30.018 --> 45:32.646
-You know that?
-You don't know Tanisha, nigga.

45:33.147 --> 45:34.940
Go get my shit.

45:57.588 --> 45:58.422
What up?

45:59.798 --> 46:02.342
Damn. His girl got a fat ass.

46:02.426 --> 46:04.803
That nigga ain't know
what to do with that.

46:54.394 --> 46:57.898
-Talk to me, Coltrane.
-Andrei's hot. Cops are on him.

46:57.981 --> 47:00.108
He's got a problem, but we ain't it.

47:02.194 --> 47:04.613
Not that-- Oh shit, nigga. Yes!

47:04.696 --> 47:06.323
Whoo! Shit!

47:06.990 --> 47:09.326
That's what I'm talking about--

47:09.409 --> 47:10.285
Whoo!

47:11.370 --> 47:12.371
Nigga.

47:14.456 --> 47:15.958
Wait till I tell these niggas.

47:19.837 --> 47:21.213
Hey, what up, loc?

47:22.965 --> 47:24.174
What's up, D?

47:26.134 --> 47:28.220
-This is Marc.
-What up, cuh?

47:28.303 --> 47:29.972
What's up?

47:31.598 --> 47:33.141
Hey! Be right back. My bad.

47:35.853 --> 47:37.020
Yo.

47:37.104 --> 47:39.815
-Now's not a good time, man.
-Hey, where you at?

47:39.898 --> 47:43.318
I left, came back. You still ain't here.
We about to fire up the grill, nigga.

47:43.402 --> 47:47.781
I'm on my way, cuh, but check it.
Hey. I just hit a lick. Clippers won.

47:47.865 --> 47:50.617
Six-leg parlay, nigga. We up!

47:50.701 --> 47:54.746
You left Big Mama on her birthday
to gamble, you fucking degenerate?

47:56.415 --> 47:57.791
Cuh. I--

47:59.459 --> 48:02.713
Man, all y'all say is, "Deon,
you can't do this. You can't do that."

48:02.796 --> 48:05.757
"If you screw up one more time"
and all the rest of that bullshit.

48:05.841 --> 48:09.386
I can't never do nothing, 'cause nobody
ever takes the time to believe in me.

48:09.469 --> 48:12.180
I got ideas, nigga. I got a plan.

48:12.264 --> 48:13.390
And after tonight,

48:13.473 --> 48:17.352
niggas gonna recognize
That Deon was right

48:17.436 --> 48:20.647
My name gonna be ringing in the streets,
on the dead homeys.

48:20.731 --> 48:21.899
Look.

48:22.441 --> 48:23.734
Look, man.

48:24.693 --> 48:28.030
All I'm asking is for you
to believe in me for once, nephew.

48:28.780 --> 48:31.074
All you had to do
was spend today with Big Mama,

48:31.158 --> 48:32.868
and you couldn't even get that right.

48:34.703 --> 48:36.496
Whatever this goddamn plan of yours is,

48:36.580 --> 48:40.125
go ahead, do that and fuck it up
and get back here so we can cut this cake.

48:46.089 --> 48:47.382
Hey, niggas!

48:49.092 --> 48:51.178
Let's do some business.

49:06.485 --> 49:07.319
What's up, baby?

49:07.903 --> 49:10.739
What time will you be home, babe?
I'm making lobster tonight.

49:11.823 --> 49:13.659
Shit, I'll be home
before you set the table.

49:13.742 --> 49:16.411
Okay. Well, I gotta go. All right, bye.

49:17.871 --> 49:20.791
Isaiah Stiles. Long time no see.

49:24.127 --> 49:25.337
Marc Johnson?

49:26.421 --> 49:28.674
How the hell are you, man?
You still in Narcotics?

49:28.757 --> 49:31.301
Hey, you know it, man.
That's why I'm here.

49:31.385 --> 49:33.303
Got a Gideon Davis flagged in your system?

49:33.387 --> 49:34.221
Yeah, why?

49:34.304 --> 49:37.808
I got him to sell me one million grams
of pharmaceutical ketamine tonight.

49:38.684 --> 49:41.436
-Stop lying. Nah, for real?
-I'm gonna meet him in an hour.

49:41.520 --> 49:44.272
Got a tracker on his car.
About to leave in a few.

49:45.273 --> 49:46.191
You wanna ride?

49:47.734 --> 49:48.568
Uh--

49:48.652 --> 49:51.238
Look, I know y'all bougie motherfuckers
at RHD work from 9 to 5…

49:51.321 --> 49:52.155
Nah.

49:52.239 --> 49:56.159
…but if it's a bad night for you,
you could have him when I'm done with him.

49:56.243 --> 49:58.662
-Nah, shut the fuck up. I'm rolling.
-Mm-hmm.

49:58.745 --> 50:01.081
If I can close this case
and lock these guys away,

50:01.164 --> 50:02.791
I might be able to have a normal life.

50:03.458 --> 50:06.378
Be half a husband for once,
you know what I mean? Shit.

50:07.212 --> 50:08.672
I'll call home, but let's roll.

50:16.138 --> 50:17.764
What could you have done, Ebony?

50:19.141 --> 50:22.728
-You did the right thing.
-I checked the security footage.

50:22.811 --> 50:25.313
He blinded your office camera,
but he didn't take anything.

50:25.397 --> 50:27.149
I did a thorough sweep.

50:33.155 --> 50:34.865
Everything's still in place.

50:37.534 --> 50:39.745
Let's go eat dinner. I'm so hungry.

50:55.052 --> 50:56.303
King's Gambit.

50:56.386 --> 50:58.430
Nice move, Stiles.

51:04.603 --> 51:07.272
I'm eating Dad's.
He not coming home anyway.

51:48.980 --> 51:49.981
Mm?

51:50.065 --> 51:53.735
Looks like Candace Stiles is on the way
to her first date with a new man.

51:53.819 --> 51:55.070
That fast? Damn.

51:55.153 --> 51:59.116
She already had one in the chamber.
I simply suggested she pull the trigger.

52:00.408 --> 52:01.451
You did good, Ebony.

52:01.535 --> 52:04.287
Oh, I did better than good.

52:04.830 --> 52:07.165
I learned that he's been unstable
since two years ago

52:07.249 --> 52:10.168
when the young detective
Emmanuel Shaw was killed.

52:12.295 --> 52:13.713
Mm.

52:16.925 --> 52:19.803
Baby, is there any way
they can tie you to Shaw?

52:20.804 --> 52:22.389
There is no way

52:22.472 --> 52:26.768
that Isaiah Stiles can connect us
to Emmanuel Shaw or any of this.

52:28.603 --> 52:29.437
We're done.

52:30.647 --> 52:33.024
-Home free.
-Yeah.

52:40.866 --> 52:42.826
Why they so fucking early?

52:43.660 --> 52:45.495
Ah, it's this nigga.

52:47.122 --> 52:49.708
-Yo! What up, cuh?
-You stole the key off my ring!

52:49.791 --> 52:51.001
I don't play that shit, D!

52:51.084 --> 52:53.587
I know you a thief,
but I ain't think you steal from me.

52:53.670 --> 52:57.382
-When I see you, we gonna squabble.
-In a couple hours, you gonna forget this.

52:57.465 --> 53:00.135
'Cause I'm about
to get us all paid, nigga.

53:07.309 --> 53:09.227
Shit!

53:10.061 --> 53:12.105
Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck!

53:20.363 --> 53:21.698
Who called in the fucking cavalry?

53:21.781 --> 53:23.783
I had to tell my lieutenant
about our meetup. My bad.

53:23.867 --> 53:26.494
-I didn't think they'd do it like this.
-Oh, man.

53:28.371 --> 53:31.374
-All right, listen up.
-I know who's running this shitshow.

53:31.458 --> 53:32.292
Come on.

53:32.375 --> 53:36.713
I want everyone in position now.
Our perp can't leave with those drugs.

53:36.796 --> 53:38.465
Hey, I need Deon alive, Murphy.

53:38.548 --> 53:40.967
-You know that fucker inside?
-He's about to be my CI.

53:41.051 --> 53:42.385
Mine too. We need him.

53:42.469 --> 53:45.472
Got the call from above. They didn't say
shit about keeping no damn perp alive.

53:45.555 --> 53:47.641
-We need them.
-I don't give a shit.

53:47.724 --> 53:49.100
Give me this.

53:49.184 --> 53:51.394
-You got five minutes.
-Shut it.

53:51.478 --> 53:52.312
Gideon.

53:53.355 --> 53:54.356
Deon!

53:55.023 --> 53:57.484
It's Lieutenant Isaiah Stiles
with the LAPD.

53:57.567 --> 54:00.654
We don't have time to fuck around.
I need you to call me right now.

54:00.737 --> 54:06.743
310-555-0129. 310-555-0129.

54:11.289 --> 54:13.959
Deon, this is Lieutenant Isaiah Stiles.
Can you hear me?

54:14.542 --> 54:15.502
Yeah. Talk, nigga.

54:15.585 --> 54:17.879
Alright, listen.
You're in a bad situation.

54:17.963 --> 54:20.257
Alright, no one else but me
can get you out of here alive.

54:20.340 --> 54:21.549
Now, are you in there alone?

54:21.633 --> 54:24.135
I'm alone, but y'all need to back up.
I ain't playing!

54:24.219 --> 54:25.929
Back up!

54:28.014 --> 54:31.351
It's my mama's birthday, cuh.
I'm just trying to feed my family.

54:32.852 --> 54:35.355
That's your natural God-given right.

54:35.438 --> 54:38.233
Listen, if you don't listen to me,
forget feeding them.

54:38.316 --> 54:39.693
They're never gonna see you again.

54:41.569 --> 54:44.656
I mean, you got two families, right?
Two ladies?

54:44.739 --> 54:46.199
Four babies total?

54:47.909 --> 54:49.035
Yeah.

54:49.828 --> 54:51.204
Four kids.

54:52.122 --> 54:56.126
Four kids, man.
You gonna let your women cry over you?

54:57.294 --> 55:00.672
You gonna let your children
grow up without their daddy?

55:01.506 --> 55:03.133
Come on, man, they need you.

55:03.216 --> 55:06.886
You know what happens to kids like that,
especially our girls.

55:18.982 --> 55:19.983
All right.

55:20.608 --> 55:21.484
I'm coming out.

55:22.152 --> 55:23.570
Give me two minutes.

55:24.904 --> 55:26.239
Two minutes!

55:26.823 --> 55:28.074
He's coming out!

55:43.423 --> 55:44.674
Yo, nephew.

55:44.758 --> 55:47.802
-Deon, get back here now.
-Darren, listen.

55:49.137 --> 55:50.013
You good, bro?

55:52.682 --> 55:53.892
Hey, yo.

55:54.893 --> 55:57.312
Yo, you remember when we was kids?

55:57.395 --> 56:02.108
I was like 9, and you was 11,
and you broke Mama's Black Jesus doll?

56:03.985 --> 56:05.153
It was a figurine.

56:05.737 --> 56:08.865
Your ears must be burning up, 'cause
me and Big Mama was talking about this.

56:09.616 --> 56:13.078
-Yo, why bring this shit up? You drunk?
-I'm not drunk.

56:13.787 --> 56:18.917
Hey, remember how she found it broken
and just started beating my ass?

56:19.000 --> 56:21.920
Even though you was the one that did it,
she just knew it was me.

56:22.003 --> 56:23.129
You ain't tell on me either.

56:23.213 --> 56:25.048
You stayed solid, like always.

56:25.548 --> 56:28.968
Didn't even cry.
What's going on, Unc? You all right?

56:29.052 --> 56:31.888
Everybody heard about
how I got whooped for ten minutes straight

56:31.971 --> 56:33.973
and didn't shed one tear.

56:35.058 --> 56:36.976
I was a legend on the block.

56:43.858 --> 56:46.111
Unc, what the fuck is going on, man?
Where you at?

56:46.194 --> 56:48.029
Just tell me where you at
and Imma come get you.

56:51.491 --> 56:53.368
You was right about me, Stro.

56:54.828 --> 56:57.205
I just keep fucking up.

56:59.040 --> 57:00.834
Hey, I do want you to know,

57:00.917 --> 57:04.629
even though you my nephew,
I've looked up to you my whole life, man.

57:04.712 --> 57:06.756
And I'm really, really proud of you.

57:07.674 --> 57:10.635
I wish I was half the dad you was, man.

57:10.718 --> 57:15.140
K-k-kiss Big Mama and my babies for me.
Tell them they daddy love 'em.

57:15.223 --> 57:17.809
Get the fuck out of here.
Nigga, you talking crazy right now.

57:17.892 --> 57:19.352
And tell Rena I tried.

57:19.436 --> 57:21.896
I really fucking tried.

57:23.440 --> 57:24.983
I'm sorry, Stro.

57:26.818 --> 57:28.736
Deon! Deon!

57:29.237 --> 57:30.071
What the fuck?

57:32.115 --> 57:35.285
Please answer the phone, Deon.
Come on, man.

57:45.086 --> 57:46.588
Baby, what's wrong?

57:49.466 --> 57:51.092
Darren?

58:33.843 --> 58:35.512
Fuck it, Stiles. You're out of time!

58:35.595 --> 58:37.263
-My men are moving in on the target.
-No!

58:37.347 --> 58:39.432
-Let's go!
-No, stop! He's coming out!

58:53.780 --> 58:55.615
-Let me see your hands!
-Deon!

58:55.698 --> 58:58.368
-Everybody hold!
-Let's see your hands right now!

58:58.451 --> 59:01.162
-Show us your hands.
-Deon, hands!

59:01.246 --> 59:02.956
Deon, look at me!

59:03.873 --> 59:06.251
Put your fucking hands
in the air right now!

59:06.334 --> 59:08.044
Hands, now!
